 "conclusion": "Two independent sensor paths (GPS course and accelerometer / speed) agree that the gyro yaw channel reads low: the logger's own GPS yaw rate is 1.205-1.215x, lateral acceleration / GPS speed 1.166-1.182x and the drawn heading rate 1.211-1.222x the gyro, on every lap of both days, while the accelerometer agrees with the GPS lateral acceleration (0.958-0.986x). So the gyro amplitude is ~14.2-18.2 % low and the drawn heading is consistent with GPS and accelerometer. Yaw leaks into the roll gyro (slope 0.154-0.164, r 0.9038-0.9349), consistent with a ~8.9-9.4 deg mount tilt, which explains only 1.2-1.4 % of the amplitude loss; the rest (a gyro scale factor / configuration) is not identified. Timing is unaffected: with the gyro rescaled the turn-in 50 % difference changes by median 0.0 s (max 0.0 s, n 104); onset-flag changes: 1."
